LangChain:

LangChain is an open-source framework for building applications (Agents) powered by large language models (LLMs). 

It provides standardized abstractions and components (chains, prompts, memory, tools integrations)  

LangChain supports multiple languages (Python / JavaScript) and lets you swap in different LLM backends, vector stores, 
data sources, etc.

Uses Of Langchain:

Chatbots / Conversational agents — maintaining context, memory, chaining operations.
Agent orchestration — linking LLM outputs with tool invocation (APIs, actions) in a chain or agent-/// one agent - output - we want to consume this out puts as input to the other agent - framework - 
Memory / State across interactions — storing conversation history or other stateful context.
Integrations with external systems — databases, vector stores, APIs, search services, etc.

