why we need framework ? why wont we  use the Models directly with out framework ?



You can absolutely work with LLMs without frameworks.
You can directly call APIs like:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(api_key="...")
response = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="gpt-4",
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": "Explain DevOps"}]
)
print(response.choices[0].message.content)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Works perfectly fine for simple one-shot queries.

But as soon as your system grows — and you need context, retrieval, tools, memory, or multiple steps — it quickly becomes complex, so we need a framework like langchain

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                            Differnece between with Framework like Langchain and wiht out Framework 


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

| Challenge                       | What Happens Without Framework                                  | How Frameworks Help                                                             |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
|       Prompt Management         | You manually write and manage dozens of prompts in code         | Provides `PromptTemplate`, parameterization, and versioning                     |
|       Multi-step Workflows      | You manually call model → parse output → call next model → etc. | `Chains` and `Agents` let you sequence or dynamically choose next steps         |
|       Context / Memory          | You store chat history manually in a DB or variable             | Provides `Memory` modules (short-term, long-term, vector memory)                |
|       Retrieval from data       | You build your own vector DB, embeddings, and similarity search | Offers built-in integration with BigQuery Vector, etc. |
|      Tool /  API Calling        | You parse JSON/text manually to decide what API to call         | LangChain handles structured “function calling” automatically                   |
|       Orchestration / Agents    | You write control logic yourself                                | Framework decides which tool/model to invoke next (“agent loop”)                |
|      Scaling  / Observability   | Hard to monitor latency, costs, or caching                      | Provides tracing (LangSmith), caching layers, retry logic                       |
|       Abstraction over LLMs     | Each vendor (OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral, Bedrock) has diff API     | Unified interface → switch model vendors easily        


