what is RAG ? Diff Between RAG and Langchain ?

RAG = Retrieval-Augmented Generation.

Definition :

It’s a technique that combines two components: a retrieval system (searching documents, knowledge bases, vector stores) + a generative model (LLM).

The idea behind : Before generating a response, the system retrieves relevant context (documents, passages) and augments the prompt or the model context
with that retrieved text. Then the LLM can generate a more informed, grounded answer rather than hallucinating.

                                                     Diff Between Langchain & RAG 


----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------




| Element    | LangChain                                                                                       | RAG                                                                               |
| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Role       | A **framework / library** for building LLM-powered apps, chaining models, memory, tools, agents | A **technique / paradigm** (retrieval + generation) to improve LLM output         |
| Scope      | Broad — supports chains, agents, memory, tool calls, etc.                                       | Focused — combining retrieval + generation for grounded responses                 |
| Usage      | You can implement RAG workflows within LangChain                                                | RAG can be used without LangChain (but LangChain helps you build RAG more easily) |
| Complexity | Orchestration, integrating many components                                                      | Mainly about retrieval + prompt augmentation                                      |
| Examples   | Agents that call APIs, maintain state, orchestrate logic                                        | A Q&A system that looks up relevant docs before responding                        |

